# No save-FILE change this session -> no --sync-save, nothing queued to pending-saves.txt. BUT
# the STATE push is DECOUPLED from the save-file gate (T1.1): a quicksave-only session writes no
# .srm yet its state must still go up, so --push-states fires online regardless. Proves the moat.
desc push: save unchanged -> no --sync-save, but decoupled --push-states still fires
invoke wrap
config paired
wifi up
sdfile+ Roms/GBA/Zelda.gba
engine 0|LOCAL=current
engine 0|RESULT mode=list-states n=0
expect_exit 0
expect_trace STOCK GBA rom=
expect_trace_absent ENGINE --sync-save
expect_trace ENGINE --push-states
expect_file_absent App/LodorSync/data/pending-saves.txt
